A||||9||Black86SE||Porting Exhaust Manifolds||||1||
Z||000000||Black86SE||11-18-2001||06:38 PM||||I am gonna port my exhaust manifolds once I get to them in my schedule of things to do. The problem is, where exactly is it on the manifolds that need to be ported? I read somewhere that it is down inside them. But I have been told that the size of factory porting is like your thumb, index finger, and little finger sizes on cyl. 1 2 3. But on mine, the holes are the same size but there is still a lot of material that could be shaved off. I was looking at my "new" manifold (the one they replaced for the recall like 2 months ago) and it looked like what I described above with them being all the same size. Maybe the original one has the different size portings? Please help with this. Plus, how would I go about porting them? Just use a tapered grinding stone on a drill? Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Black 1986 V6 SE<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS<BR>AIM ScreenName: Black86se||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnF||11-18-2001||07:21 PM||||Good question.  I'll bump this one because I need the same answer.<P>Experts answer, please!||||reg||5
Z||000002||Phil||11-18-2001||08:39 PM||||The restriction is located where the tube from the exhaust port joins the long part of the manifold. If you look down into the tube you should see part of the long tube still showing in 2 of the 3 ports, this is what should be removed. Also have the flange plate  welded to the short tubes on the outside of the flange and grind off the approx. 1/8" original weld bead that is on the inner side||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||11-18-2001||09:01 PM||||Phil is right. Weld all the flanges to the pipes. Then looking down into each pipe you will see a ewstriction where they join. Its the hole in the main runner that is smaller that each tube. There is also weld bead and spatter that I clean up when I do mine. I used a carbide burr on a die grinder the a cartridge rool for the final cleanup and smooth.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DR650SE||11-18-2001||09:12 PM||||Trust me.  Once you take them off and look in.   You know whats up.  You'll see the obvious.  I have a pic of mine not ported from when i replaced them but I can't scan.  Don't worry.  When you guys look you will see the problems.  Can't miss it.  Honest<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000005||DR650SE||11-18-2001||09:13 PM||||Trust me.  Once you take them off and look in.   You know whats up.  You'll see the obvious.  I have a pic of mine not ported from when i replaced them but I can't scan.  Don't worry.  When you guys look you will see the problems.  Can't miss it.  Honest<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
